.SS "void p8est_search_reorder (\fBp8est_t\fP * p4est, int skip_levels, \fBp8est_search_reorder_t\fP reorder_fn, \fBp8est_search_local_t\fP pre_quadrant_fn, \fBp8est_search_local_t\fP post_quadrant_fn, \fBp8est_search_local_t\fP point_fn, sc_array_t * points)"

.PP
Run a depth-first traversal, optionally filtering search points\&. There are three main differences to \fBp8est_search_local\fP :
.PP
.IP "\(bu" 2
Before beginning the recursion, we call the \fIreorder_fn\fP callback with an index array enumerating the local tree roots\&. The callback may permute its entries to define the order of trees to traverse\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
After the pre-quadrant callback and its point callbacks, the \fIreorder\fP callback is passed an index array to relevant child numbers of the branch quadrant, ordered but possibly non-contiguous\&. It may permute these to indicate the sequence of the children to traverse\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
The post-quadrant callback is executed after the recursion returns\&. Even for leaves, it is called whenever the pre-callback returned true\&. Even called when all points have been unmatched by the point callback\&.
.PP
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fI\fBp4est\fP\fP The forest to be searched\&. 
.br
\fIskip_levels\fP If true and there is a search window that contains a single descendant, or if all quadrants in the search window are descendants of one child of it, skip the intermediate recursion levels\&. 
.br
\fIreorder_fn\fP Called with \fIquadrants\fP input array containing either the local tree roots or a set of siblings\&. The array may be permuted on output to define the order of traversal of the quadrants\&. May be NULL to omit reordering, always recurse\&. If not NULL and it returns true, don't recurse\&. 
.br
\fIpre_quadrant_fn\fP As in \fBp8est_search_local\fP, pre-order callback\&. If the pre-callback returns false, recursion stops\&. If it returns true, recursion continues\&. The \fIquadrant\fP argument is the same pre and post\&. 
.br
\fIpost_quadrant_fn\fP As in \fBp8est_search_local\fP, post-order callback\&. It is called whenever the pre-callback returns true\&. The \fIquadrant\fP argument is the same pre and post\&. 
.br
\fIpoint_fn\fP As in \fBp8est_search_local\fP\&. 
.br
\fIpoints\fP As in \fBp8est_search_local\fP\&. May be NULL to use quadrant callbacks only\&. Otherwise, if no points remain for a particular search quadrant, the recursion stops even if the quadrant callback indicates to continue\&. This behavior can be prevented by always keeping one bogus point around\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "void p8est_split_array (sc_array_t * array, int level, size_t indices[])"

.PP
Split an array of quadrants by the children of an ancestor\&. Given a sorted \fBarray\fP of quadrants that have a common ancestor at level \fBlevel\fP, compute the \fBindices\fP of the first quadrant in each of the common ancestor's children at level \fBlevel\fP + 1\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIarray\fP The sorted array of quadrants of level > \fBlevel\fP\&. 
.br
\fIlevel\fP The level at which there is a common ancestor\&. 
.br
\fIindices\fP The indices of the first quadrant in each of the ancestors's children, plus an additional index on the end\&. The quadrants of \fBarray\fP that are descendants of child i have indices between indices[i] and indices[i + 1] - 1\&. If indices[i] = indices[i+1], this indicates that no quadrant in the array is contained in child i\&. 
.RE
.PP

